{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789661309,"nonce":"SILGu+EImoYbTr1e1u4sF4zPvy4=","title":"Schema engine: field kinds, values, categories, validation","message":"Requirement: just configurable enough to squarely represent Jira's native model and Linear's. Resolve that as a fixed set of field *kinds* with configurable *values*:\n\n- `enum-with-category` — status. Categories are fixed: backlog / unstarted / started / completed / canceled (Linear's set; Jira statusCategory To Do/In Progress/Done maps onto it). Statuses within a category are configurable.\n- `ordinal-enum` — priority (Linear none..urgent, Jira Lowest..Highest).\n- `text`, `number` (estimate: points), `date` (start/target/due), `identity` (assignee).\n- Issue *type* is an ordered list (hierarchy levels) with allowed-parent rules; see relations.\n\nTooling (kanban, Gantt, report) keys off kinds and categories, never names. Validation produces actionable errors (`status \"done\" not in schema; valid: ...`) because agents are the main caller.","files":null},{"type":9,"timestamp":1789661309,"nonce":"7M31KsT3Yypp3ZpmGlgXLo3RksM=","key":"type","value":"task"},{"type":9,"timestamp":1789661309,"nonce":"ICh/OwW4ZaqryjokE9tOBs2SItE=","key":"status","value":"to-do"}]}